      "problem": "What is the distance between the points $(-\\sqrt{3},2\\sqrt{3})$ and $(3\\sqrt{3},5\\sqrt{3})?$",
      "worked_solution": "In this case, we have ${{(-\\sqrt{3},2\\sqrt{3})}_{⏟}}_{\\text{(}{x}_{1}\\text{,}\\,{y}_{1})}$ and ${{(3\\sqrt{3},5\\sqrt{3})}_{⏟}}_{\\text{(}{x}_{2}\\text{,}\\,{y}_{2})}.$\nSo, the distance $d$ can be calculated using the distance formula, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =\\sqrt{({x}_{2}-{x}_{1})^{2}+({y}_{2}-{y}_{1})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{(3\\sqrt{3}-(-\\sqrt{3}))}^{2}+{(5\\sqrt{3}-2\\sqrt{3})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(4\\sqrt{3})^{2}+(3\\sqrt{3})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16(3)+9(3)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{48+27} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{75} \\\\  & =5\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
